sequenceDiagram
    participant KServe as KServe/ModelMesh Agent
    participant Proxy as kube-rbac-proxy<br/>8443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Gzip as GzipRequestMiddleware
    participant Consumer as Consumer Endpoint<br/>8080/TCP HTTP (loopback)
    participant Storage as Storage Interface<br/>(PVC HDF5 / MariaDB)
    participant Scheduler as PrometheusScheduler<br/>(asyncio, 30s)
    participant Core as Core Algorithms<br/>(drift, fairness)
    participant Publisher as PrometheusPublisher<br/>(OpenMetrics registry)
    participant Prom as Prometheus Server
    participant Client as Client<br/>(Dashboard / Notebook)
    participant Upload as Data Upload Endpoint

    rect rgb(230, 245, 255)
        Note over KServe,Storage: Flow 1: KServe Inference Data Ingestion
        KServe->>Proxy: POST / (KServe CloudEvent)<br/>or POST /consumer/kserve/v2 (ModelMesh protobuf)<br/>HTTPS TLS 1.2+, Kubernetes RBAC
        Proxy->>Consumer: Forward to 127.0.0.1:8080<br/>HTTP (loopback, no auth)
        Consumer->>Gzip: Decompress if gzip-encoded
        Gzip-->>Consumer: Decompressed payload
        Consumer->>Consumer: Reconcile input/output pairs<br/>by inference ID
        Consumer->>Storage: Persist reconciled data<br/>(HDF5 on PVC or MariaDB 3306/TCP)
        Storage-->>Consumer: Ack
    end

    rect rgb(230, 255, 230)
        Note over Scheduler,Prom: Flow 2: Scheduled Metric Computation
        Scheduler->>Storage: Load model datasets<br/>(every 30s default)
        Storage-->>Scheduler: Model inference data
        Scheduler->>Core: Compute drift metrics<br/>(KS-Test, CompareMeans, etc.)
        Core-->>Scheduler: Metric values
        Scheduler->>Core: Compute fairness metrics<br/>(SPD, DIR)
        Core-->>Scheduler: Metric values
        Scheduler->>Publisher: Publish trustyai_* gauges<br/>to Prometheus client registry
        Prom->>Proxy: GET /q/metrics<br/>HTTPS, Kubernetes RBAC
        Proxy->>Publisher: Forward to 127.0.0.1:8080
        Publisher-->>Proxy: OpenMetrics response
        Proxy-->>Prom: Metrics payload
    end

    rect rgb(255, 245, 230)
        Note over Client,Storage: Flow 3: Data Upload
        Client->>Proxy: POST /data/upload<br/>HTTPS TLS 1.2+, Kubernetes RBAC
        Proxy->>Upload: Forward to 127.0.0.1:8080<br/>HTTP (loopback)
        Upload->>Gzip: Decompress if gzip-encoded
        Gzip-->>Upload: Decompressed payload
        Upload->>Upload: Reconcile input/output pairs
        Upload->>Storage: Persist to PVC/MariaDB
        Storage-->>Upload: Ack
        Upload-->>Proxy: 200 OK
        Proxy-->>Client: Response
    end
